From: LuckFox Yocto BSP <noreply@luckfox.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rk3506: prioritize distro boot over boot_fit

The default RKIMG_BOOTCOMMAND for RK3506 only tries boot_fit and
boot_android, with no fallback to distro_bootcmd. This prevents
booting standard Linux distributions that use extlinux.conf or
boot.scr on a FAT/ext4 boot partition.

Reorder the boot sequence to try distro_bootcmd FIRST, before
boot_fit. The vendor boot_fit command may hang if it encounters
unexpected data on eMMC, preventing fallback to distro boot.
By trying distro boot first, we ensure extlinux.conf-based boot
works reliably while still falling back to boot_fit/boot_android
for vendor firmware compatibility.

Signed-off-by: LuckFox Yocto BSP <noreply@luckfox.com>
---
 include/configs/rk3506_common.h | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/include/configs/rk3506_common.h
+++ b/include/configs/rk3506_common.h
@@ -116,11 +116,13 @@
 #undef RKIMG_BOOTCOMMAND
 #ifdef CONFIG_FIT_SIGNATURE
 #define RKIMG_BOOTCOMMAND		\
-	"boot_fit;"
+	"run distro_bootcmd;"		\
+	"boot_fit;"
 #else
 #define RKIMG_BOOTCOMMAND		\
-	"boot_fit;"			\
-	"boot_android ${devtype} ${devnum};"
+	"run distro_bootcmd;"		\
+	"boot_fit;"			\
+	"boot_android ${devtype} ${devnum};"
 #endif

 #endif
